13:T8a4,In a major and closely watched legal development, Ingham County District Court Judge Kristen D.  Simmons has formally dismissed criminal charges against 15 individuals who had been accused of participating in a plan to falsely certify Donald Trump as the winner of Michigan’s 2020 presidential election.  These defendants, several of whom are prominent figures within Michigan’s Republican Party, faced charges including forgery and conspiracy stemming from their submission of documents asserting that they were the state’s legitimate electors for Trump, despite the clear and decisive victory of Joe Biden in the state during the 2020 election.  The charges arose after state prosecutors initiated an investigation into actions that were widely criticized as attempts to undermine the certified election results and subvert the democratic process.  Judge Simmons’ ruling emphasized that the prosecution had failed to demonstrate that the defendants acted with fraudulent intent, noting instead that evidence suggested these individuals genuinely believed that irregularities had occurred during the election and that they were exercising what they viewed as their constitutional rights.  In her ruling, Judge Simmons detailed the difficulty in establishing beyond a reasonable doubt that the defendants knowingly attempted to commit a criminal act, highlighting that personal belief in alleged election issues complicated the legal analysis and ultimately undermined the state’s case.  The dismissal represents a significant setback for the state prosecutors who had invested considerable resources into the investigation and legal proceedings, and it is emblematic of a broader trend in battleground states such as Arizona, Georgia, and Nevada, where similar prosecutions have faced challenges in proving fraudulent intent, as defendants often claim to have acted in good faith based on their understanding of election procedures and perceived irregularities.  Legal experts analyzing the ruling note that while the actions of the defendants were politically charged and generated widespread criticism, the judicial system must focus on intent and evidence rather than perceptions or public outrage.4:[["$","$Lf",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"NewsArticle\",\"mainEntityOfPage\":{\"@type\":\"WebPage\",\"@id\":\"https://www.pressorahub.com/us/michigan-dismissal-highlights-challenges-in-prosecuting-2020-fake-electors/\"},\"headline\":\"Michigan Dismissal Shows Problems for Prosecutors of 2020 Fake Electors\",\"description\":\"A judge in Michigan has dismissed charges against 15 people who were trying to falsify Donald Trump as the winner of the 2020 presidential election. The judge determined there was no fraudulent intent.\",\"image\":\"/images/michigan-fake-electors-case-dismissal.webp\",\"author\":{\"@type\":\"Person\",\"name\":\"Lauren Jacobs\",\"url\":\"https://www.pressorahub.com/our-team/\"},\"publisher\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"PressoraHub\",\"logo\":{\"@type\":\"ImageObject\",\"url\":\"https://www.pressorahub.com/images/pressorahub-icon.webp\"}},\"datePublished\":\"2025-06-18T00:00:00.000Z\",\"dateModified\":\"2025-06-18T00:00:00.000Z\"}"}}],["$","$L10",null,{"breadcrumbTitle":"Michigan Dismissal Shows Problems for Prosecutors of 2020 Fake Electors","category":"us","children":["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","section",null,{"className":"post-layout-1 padding","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"container","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"top-content","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"post-card single-card","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"post-content","children":[["$","$L11",null,{"title":"michigan-dismissal-highlights-challenges-in-prosecuting-2020-fake-electors","href":"/us","className":"card-btn bg-green","children":"us"}],["$","h1",null,{"className":"title","style":{"lineHeight":1.3},"children":"Michigan Dismissal Shows Problems for Prosecutors of 2020 Fake Electors"}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"post-list","children":[["$","li",null,{"className":"author","children":["by ",["$","span",null,{"children":"Lauren Jacobs"}]]}],["$","li",null,{"className":"date","children":"October 13, 2025"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"children":"A judge in Michigan has dismissed charges against 15 people who were trying to falsify Donald Trump as the winner of the 2020 presidential election. The judge determined there was no fraudulent intent."}]]}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"post-social","children":["$","ul",null,{"className":"social-list d-flex align-items-center","children":[["$","li",null,{}],["$","li",null,{"children":["$","$L11",null,{"href":"https://www.instagram.com/laur.enjacobs001/","className":"instagram","title":"instagram","children":["$","i",null,{"className":"lab la-instagram"}]}]}],["$","li",null,{"children":["$","$L11",null,{"href":"https://medium.com/@lauren_jacobs","className":"","style":{"border":""},"children":["$","i",null,{"className":"lab la-medium"}]}]}],["$","li",null,{"children":["$","$L11",null,{"href":"https://substack.com/@laurenjacobs672308","className":"pinterest","children":["$","svg",null,{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"20","height":"15","viewBox":"0 0 256 256","children":["$","g",null,{"transform":"scale(5.12,5.12)","children":[["$","path",null,{"d":"M43,11h-35v-6h35z"}],["$","path",null,{"d":"M43,19h-35v-6h35z"}],["$","path",null,{"d":"M43,44.805l-17.016,-10.636l-17.984,10.579v-23.748h35z"}]]}]}]}]}]]}]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"row","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"col-lg-8","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"post-layout-content","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"layout-thumb mb-30","children":["$","$L12",null,{"title":"Michigan Dismissal Shows Problems for Prosecutors of 2020 Fake Electors","src":"/images/michigan-fake-electors-case-dismissal.webp","alt":"Michigan Dismissal Shows Problems for Prosecutors of 2020 Fake Electors","width":1200,"height":800,"priority":true,"style":{"width":"100%","height":"auto"}}]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","p","0",{"className":"layout-desc","style":{"marginBottom":"1rem"},"children":"$13"}],"$L14","$L15","$L16"]}],"$L17","$L18"]}]}],"$L19"]}]]}]}],"$L1a"]}]}]]
